{"text": " Missing one day doesn't break a habit, missing the second day does. Say you run three times a week and on Wednesday you missed it, what you do next decides the habit. Most people try to catch up, two runs on Thursday, it feels heavy so they skip that two, now one misses two. One don't double up, just the next run at its normal size. Two, book it now, Thursday 7 am in your calendar like a meeting. Three, if Thursday goes wrong, 10 minutes counts, zero doesn't. Miss once, that's life, never miss twice, send this to someone who just missed a day. That's what Demure is for, you archive your dream today so you can see it tomorrow and break it down into small steps you can actually do. Follow for one fix a day, next your Sunday cleanup in 10 minutes a night. If you want to try it out, I've put the link in the bio.", "segments": [{"id": 0, "seek": 0, "start": 0.0, "end": 5.2, "text": " Missing one day doesn't break a habit, missing the second day does. Say you run three times a week", "tokens": [50363, 25639, 530, 1110, 1595, 470, 2270, 257, 7947, 11, 4814, 262, 1218, 1110, 857, 13, 13816, 345, 1057, 1115, 1661, 257, 1285, 50619], "temperature": 0.0, "avg_logprob": -0.11510654323357196, "compression_ratio": 1.6418439716312057, "no_speech_prob": 0.004393371753394604, "words": [{"word": " Missing", "start": 0.0, "end": 0.38, "probability": 0.8853536248207092}, {"word": " one", "start": 0.38, "end": 0.68, "probability": 0.9381915330886841}, {"word": " day", "start": 0.68, "end": 0.9, "probability": 0.9933962821960449}, {"word": " doesn't", "start": 0.9, "end": 1.22, "probability": 0.979715883731842}, {"word": " break", "start": 1.22, "end": 1.4, "probability": 0.9961386322975159}, {"word": " a", "start": 1.4, "end": 1.56, "probability": 0.9978750944137573}, {"word": " habit,", "start": 1.56, "end": 1.84, "probability": 0.9983299374580383}, {"word": " missing", "start": 2.16, "end": 2.3, "probability": 0.9616634845733643}, {"word": " the", "start": 2.3, "end": 2.52,